BIRKENSTOCK FOR LONG OVERSEAS TRIP?

5418 says...

> Hi all,
>
> I'm planning a trip to the US going around by train and to Cologne,
> Germany for about 2-3 months overall.  I think I'll take my
> Birkenstock "Boston" with me.  It's the model with the front part
> of the shoes all

> covered but the back part opened just like their sandals.  Hope you
> can imagine the picture.  I'd like an opinion about this.  Has
> anyone taken these shoes to travel before?  Because they have no
> back part, I'm afraid they would slip out while walking fast.
>
> Thanks,
> PP

Fascinating question, and well worth the cross-posting.

Fortunately for you, that specific Birkenstock shoe is known to function
in exactly the same way whether you are at home, in Germany, or
traveling around the US.  (Of course, I am assuming you live in the
northern hemisphere; if you live in Australia, that would of course be
different because of the direction of the Coriolis force.)  Anyway, you
could just try walking fast around the block where you live and see if
it comes off.  This is what is known as 'research' in the international
scientific community.

R. Kalia <kalia@sludge.phys.nwu.edu> [rec.travel.misc]
